<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How Redbarn Ventures collects, uses and protects personal data on redbarn.ventures." lead="Last updated 20 November 2026. This policy explains what personal data we collect through this website, why we collect it and the rights you have.">
  <section><h2>Who we are</h2><p>Redbarn Ventures ("Redbarn", "we", "us") is a design and growth studio providing brand, website, marketing, SEO, consultancy and corporate materials services. We are responsible for the personal data described in this policy. You can contact us about privacy at any time at <a href={`mailto:${E}`}>{E}</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What we collect</h2><p>We only collect the information you choose to give us and the minimum technical data needed to run the website:</p><ul><li><b>Contact form:</b> your name, email address, company, website, the services you are interested in and your message.</li><li><b>Email and WhatsApp:</b> anything you send us directly, including attachments and your phone number if you contact us on WhatsApp.</li><li><b>Technical data:</b> our hosting provider processes IP addresses and request logs to deliver and protect the website.</li></ul><p>We do not use advertising trackers or analytics cookies on this website.</p></section>
  <section><h2>How we use it</h2><ul><li>To reply to your enquiry and prepare a proposal if you ask for one.</li><li>To deliver services if we work together, including invoicing and project communication.</li><li>To keep the website secure and working properly.</li></ul><p>We never sell your data and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your consent.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Legal basis</h2><p>Under applicable data protection law, including the GDPR where it applies, we rely on your consent when you contact us, on our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries and running our business, and on the performance of a contract when we work together.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Service providers</h2><p>We use a small number of trusted providers to operate this website: a hosting and content-delivery provider, an email provider, and a form-delivery service that forwards contact-form messages to our inbox. If you choose to contact us on WhatsApp, your message is processed by WhatsApp under its own privacy policy. Each provider processes data only as needed to provide its service. Where data is transferred internationally, appropriate safeguards are used.</p></section>
  <section><h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>We keep enquiries for as long as needed to respond and for up to three years afterwards, unless we start working together, in which case project records are kept for as long as required for legal, tax and accounting purposes.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your rights</h2><p>You can ask us to access, correct, delete or export your personal data, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to withdraw consent at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${E}`}>{E}</a> and we will respond promptly. You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Cookies</h2><p>This website does not set advertising or analytics cookies. Our hosting provider may set strictly necessary technical cookies to protect the site from abuse. Fonts are hosted on our own servers, so no font provider receives your data.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be available on this page, with the date of the last update shown at the top.</p></section>
</Legal>
